# Design note

A simple templating language.

## Template table

a declarative syntax for definintion structured text.

```
[div
   id="wrapper"
   display="grid cols-2 gap-1 ai-center ji-left jc-center"
   display="(width < 750px) cols-1"

   a plain text

   "a quoted text"

   (expression)
   (expression arg)

   \( literal parenthesis
   \[ literal bracket

   \(text surrounded in parenthesis)
   \[text surrounded in square bracket]

   [p
      a block text
      [span an inline text ]
      [em emphasised text ]
      [strong important text ]
      ]
   ]

   [code
      lang="js"

      function load() {
         document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoad", () => {})
         }

      ]

   [:keyword
      text
      [element]
      (expression)
      ]

   To render as an element, there most be no space between the [ and the tag name
   [ not an element; just some text in brackets ]

   To render as an expression, there most be no space between the ( and the expression
   ( not an expression; just some text in parenthesis )
```
